{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars","id":1493046,"title":"Void Spirit Familiars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-14T00:50:25-07:00","id":1493046,"title":"Void Spirit Familiars","content":"Void Spirits are more of a Werewolf thing, but so what. What are some interesting potential ramifications that could occur from a Mage binding a Void Spirit as a Familiar, beyond the local Werewolf pack suddenly gunning for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T01:18:00-07:00","id":1493047,"title":"","content":"Remind me, does that refer to any spirit from beyond the Moon, or just the ones that inhabit the empty space?<br /> <br /> I can imagine it's the kind of familiar you'll want to keep a tight leash on, lest it start using its powers to create some really weird effects on its environment. I'd say that if it's a Thyrsus or other mage who uses Spirit a lot, you're potentially taking a hit to your standing in the Shadow that can make things a bit more tricky over there. Even if they're not generally hostile, I can see them making themselves less available or forthcoming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T01:18:08-07:00","id":1493048,"title":"","content":"The most readily thinkable feature would be that the Spirit Blight features get applied to the mage\u2019s Long-Term Nimbus, rather than a distinct area. Or maybe they get applied within any Demesnes the mage erects after setting the Familiar bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T01:25:20-07:00","id":1493049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars?p=1493047#post1493047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind me, does that refer to any spirit from beyond the Moon, or just the ones that inhabit the empty space?</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>think</i> it's technically any that come from beyond the Moon's orbit, excluding Helions. The &quot;common&quot; ones are stuff like light-eaters and Martian invaders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars?p=1493047#post1493047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can imagine it's the kind of familiar you'll want to keep a tight leash on, lest it start using its powers to create some really weird effects on its environment. I'd say that if it's a Thyrsus or other mage who uses Spirit a lot, you're potentially taking a hit to your standing in the Shadow that can make things a bit more tricky over there. Even if they're not generally hostile, I can see them making themselves less available or forthcoming.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars?p=1493048#post1493048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most readily thinkable feature would be that the Spirit Blight features get applied to the mage\u2019s Long-Term Nimbus, rather than a distinct area. Or maybe they get applied within any Demesnes the mage erects after setting the Familiar bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it'd be like shackling inchoate madness to yourself and just praying it doesn't overwhelm you...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T02:16:33-07:00","id":1493050,"title":"","content":"On a second read of NH:SM, I wonder if the Alien Symbolism feature apply to Awakened magic too. The wording seems to suggest so.<br /> <br /> If so, this may be one reason why mages would seek out a void spirit or mulhithim as a Familiar; extra safety from having your Familiar somehow manipulated. Because as all mages know, <i>surely</i> any disaster relevant to your Familiar would be caused by third parties outside your intent, since <i>of course</i> you have everything that's 'yours' under your control...<br /> <br /> Wonder if the Thrice-Great have anything to say about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T03:40:55-07:00","id":1493052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars?p=1493050#post1493050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder if the Thrice-Great have anything to say about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point, what exactly are those planetary courts they associate with? Are they Goetia, spirit courts of mortal perceptions of astrology, or out-and-out extraterrestrial spirits? They have to go to the edge of the Astral for a lot of their gimmicks...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 09-14-2022, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T04:24:01-07:00","id":1493054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars?p=1493052#post1493052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good point, what exactly are those planetary courts they associate with? Are they Goetia, courts of mortal perceptions of astrology, or out-and-out extrasolar spirits? They have to go to the edge of the Astral for a lot of their gimmicks...</div> </div> </div> </div>My headcanon is that they indeed mingle with the mulhithim of the five major astrological planets, plus rogue Helions and Lunes. Mages being mages, the Hermetics are nothing but subservient to their spirit allies, and are quite willing to be manipulative and exploitative to their \u2018teachers\u2019 and \u2018patrons\u2019 if given the chance \u2014 but they are long and strong allies nonetheless. A rude shock indeed to any Uratha who think of mulhithim invasions as sporadic or isolated events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T07:59:27-07:00","id":1493061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars?p=1493049#post1493049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it'd be like shackling inchoate madness to yourself and just praying it doesn't overwhelm you...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a two dot Spirit spell to make everything they might attempt on you a Clash of Wills, and spirits roll Rank to try winning that. A mage who made their own Familiar has no excuse being vulnerable to it.<br /> <br /> Especially if it's the type that has been fettered. Hell, teach a spirit some obedience by withholding its Essence.<br /> <br /> DaveB had made comments to the effect that the spirits the Thrice-Great make use of are actually supposed to be space stuff as seen in Werewolf. I would reconcile a bit with original portrayal with an idea that they know planetary Shadows a bit better than most terrestrial beings and can filter out the ones that fit a bit more with astrology, but there's still a lot of dangerous stuff they're dealing with.<br /> <br /> And I'd still have it in Second Edition that they're a Spirit Legacy rather than using the Astral representations.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't really have it that a familiar can put something through the Nimbus unless it's already a being that interacts with such a thing, and I don't think that's necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T13:35:45-07:00","id":1493069,"title":"","content":"Some rare spirits can traverse beyond the Shadow Realm. Maybe they\u2019re <i>influenced</i> by astrology,these planetary spirit-courts, rather dominated by astrology?<br /> <br /> Then again, maybe the Thrice-Great are hanging out with Cthulhu and too arrogant to realize the danger they\u2019re in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T14:10:59-07:00","id":1493071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars?p=1493069#post1493069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, maybe the Thrice-Great are hanging out with Cthulhu and too arrogant to realize the danger they\u2019re in?</div> </div> </div> </div>That fits pretty well with my mental image of them, honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T17:21:25-07:00","id":1493083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars?p=1493047#post1493047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind me, does that refer to any spirit from beyond the Moon, or just the ones that inhabit the empty space?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mulhithim \u2014 the planetary angels \u2014 share some qualities with true void spirits, but specifically aren't <i>as</i> intrinsically ruinous to the Shadow's ecology as void leviathans and lesser void-spirits usually are; they speak First Tongue normally and don't trigger spiritual blights in the area around them, but they're explicitly mentioned in the rule for being resistant or immune to terrestrial spiritual powers and aren't called out as not subject to the dietary complications of being from literally out-of-this-world.<br /> <br /> It is worth noting that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131223#post1131223\">the main instance where Dave mentioned the Thrice-Great in the context of 2e</a> involved them dealing with &quot;spirits of the night sky,&quot; and also that the particularly esoteric nature of both the lore that would theoretically allow one to bind a spirit from the Void Beyond and the lore that the Thrice-Great deal with means there's not much of a contradiction in terms with &quot;extraterrestrial spirits are largely immune to ritual binding&quot; and &quot;the Thrice-Great bargain their way up the planetary courts' hierarchies for power and influence.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T18:04:28-07:00","id":1493088,"title":"","content":"\u201cBinding\u201d is different from \u201cbargaining\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T05:28:58-07:00","id":1493108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars?p=1493083#post1493083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mulhithim \u2014 the planetary angels \u2014 share some qualities with true void spirits, but specifically aren't <i>as</i> intrinsically ruinous to the Shadow's ecology as void leviathans and lesser void-spirits usually are; they speak First Tongue normally and don't trigger spiritual blights in the area around them, but they're explicitly mentioned in the rule for being resistant or immune to terrestrial spiritual powers and aren't called out as not subject to the dietary complications of being from literally out-of-this-world.<br /> <br /> It is worth noting that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130979-the-third-supplement-for-mage-2ed?p=1131223#post1131223\">the main instance where Dave mentioned the Thrice-Great in the context of 2e</a> involved them dealing with &quot;spirits of the night sky,&quot; and also that the particularly esoteric nature of both the lore that would theoretically allow one to bind a spirit from the Void Beyond and the lore that the Thrice-Great deal with means there's not much of a contradiction in terms with &quot;extraterrestrial spirits are largely immune to ritual binding&quot; and &quot;the Thrice-Great bargain their way up the planetary courts' hierarchies for power and influence.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would wonder if the idea of immunity to terrestrial spiritual powers is predicated mostly on the particular lore surrounding the interconnectedness of the Shadow and particularly its basis for how rites work, which I found you very effectively described in another recent thread. I'm not sure if such a thing would necessarily extend to Supernal magic, unless the Werewolf book describing them specifically said it did.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Dark Eras 2 went and described several Mysteries in terms of particular circumstances that kind of inhibited or shut down Supernal spells altogether, so there would also be precedent for the idea that mages encounter these things, find that they're less pliant to the Spirit Arcanum than they've come to expect, and it becomes both a source of caution and inquiry.<br /> <br /> I will consider that, as far as the Thrice-Great goes, this can probably be ripe as one of those examples where Second Edition Legacies specifically are not written verbotim from their original sources, a way of updating them to be more consistent with ways that the description of the extraterrestrial Shadow has been elaborated upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T17:47:16-07:00","id":1493137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars?p=1493108#post1493108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would wonder if the idea of immunity to terrestrial spiritual powers is predicated mostly on the particular lore surrounding the interconnectedness of the Shadow and particularly its basis for how rites work, which I found you very effectively described in another recent thread. I'm not sure if such a thing would necessarily extend to Supernal magic, unless the Werewolf book describing them specifically said it did.</div> </div> </div> </div>The specific wording is that, in addition to adding their Rank to rolls to contest supernatural powers from entities native to &quot;this world and its Shadow,&quot; they're not usually affected by &quot;witchcraft and ritual magic,&quot; which it specifies includes werewolf rites because this is a Night Horrors book for Werewolf antagonists presenting this information. The workarounds include the theoretical possibility of entirely new rites capable of binding or banishing void spirits, or the trick particular to werewolf rites that is adding a Void symbol to the rite's performance and making the effects of a failed roll in the extended action more dire.<br /> <br /> Worth noting that, while they're not the same thing, the idigam have blanket immunity to powers that would &quot;command them, master them, or reshape their abilities,&quot; including &quot;Gifts, rites, and the witchcraft of other beings,&quot; and they get their name from the more famous set of them having been banished to the Moon during the time of Pangaea. There may not be an intrinsic &quot;sympathetic magic beyond the lunar sphere doesn't work&quot; element of the cosmology anymore, but void spirits are made from resonances largely divorced from the Earthly ecosystem and its conceptual derivations, which seems as good an explanation as any for Shadow-stuff that Luna didn't manage to keep away being an out-of-context problem for anyone who's got to deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T19:07:50-07:00","id":1493141,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve always wondered if idigam were void-spirits. I\u2019m not so sure, anymore, that that\u2019s what they were. They may be void-spirits now, though, after millennia on the moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T19:10:57-07:00","id":1493142,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly certain they weren't <i>before</i>, but the argument could certainly be made that they've assimilated at least a few scraps of Void symbolism <i>now</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T19:33:13-07:00","id":1493143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars?p=1493142#post1493142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly certain they weren't <i>before</i>, but the argument could certainly be made that they've assimilated at least a few scraps of Void symbolism <i>now</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assimiliation is a tad antithetical to an entity distinct for it's fluidity of being outside of their periods of coalesence, but given that they have access to the dread power most capable of calling down the void, there is room to argue that there's resonance between the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T23:33:39-07:00","id":1493153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1493046-void-spirit-familiars?p=1493137#post1493137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The specific wording is that, in addition to adding their Rank to rolls to contest supernatural powers from entities native to &amp;quot;this world and its Shadow,&amp;quot; they're not usually affected by &amp;quot;witchcraft and ritual magic,&amp;quot; which it specifies includes werewolf rites because this is a Night Horrors book for Werewolf antagonists presenting this information. The workarounds include the theoretical possibility of entirely new rites capable of binding or banishing void spirits, or the trick particular to werewolf rites that is adding a Void symbol to the rite's performance and making the effects of a failed roll in the extended action more dire.<br /> <br /> Worth noting that, while they're not the same thing, the idigam have blanket immunity to powers that would &amp;quot;command them, master them, or reshape their abilities,&amp;quot; including &amp;quot;Gifts, rites, and the witchcraft of other beings,&amp;quot; and they get their name from the more famous set of them having been banished to the Moon during the time of Pangaea. There may not be an intrinsic &amp;quot;sympathetic magic beyond the lunar sphere doesn't work&amp;quot; element of the cosmology anymore, but void spirits are made from resonances largely divorced from the Earthly ecosystem and its conceptual derivations, which seems as good an explanation as any for Shadow-stuff that Luna didn't manage to keep away being an out-of-context problem for anyone who's got to deal with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the other way to make this feel consistent with Mage is to imagine some beings running on the equivalent of Imperial magic pitted against dispellation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}